{"format":"openchronology","version":1,"title":"Star Wars: an unofficial chronology, canon and Legends","description":"The galaxy far, far away from the first Jedi to the Legacy era, dated in years before and after the Battle of Yavin (BBY and ABY). Each moment is tagged by its continuity (canon, Legends, both for the original six films, or non-canon for Visions) and by the medium that tells it (film, TV, novel, comic or video game), and colored by medium; eras are shown as spans.\n\nAn unofficial fan chronology. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Lucasfilm or The Walt Disney Company; summaries are our own.","presentation":{"mode":"custom","unit":"","ruler":{"kind":"steps","steps":["31557600/1","157788000/1","315576000/1","1577880000/1","3155760000/1","15778800000/1","31557600000/1","157788000000/1","315576000000/1"]},"scale":"1/1","origin":"0/1","source":"function print(time: Rational, api: TimeAPI): string {\n  const x = api.div(time, api.rational(\"31557600\"));\n  const fine = api.hasView() ? api.compare(api.labelResolution(), api.rational(\"31557600\")) < 0 : true;\n  const before = api.compare(x, api.rational(\"0\")) <= 0;\n  const y = api.abs(x);\n  return (fine ? api.decimal(y, 2) : api.decimal(y, 0)) + (before ? \" BBY\" : \" ABY\");\n}\nfunction parse(text: string, api: TimeAPI): Rational {\n  const t = api.upper(api.trim(text));\n  const before = api.endsWith(t, \"BBY\");\n  const n = api.parseNumber(api.trim(api.stripSuffix(api.stripSuffix(t, \"BBY\"), \"ABY\")));\n  return api.mul(before ? api.neg(n) : n, api.rational(\"31557600\"));\n}","version":1,"offsetMinutes":0,"significantDigits":6},"plugins":[{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"rich-text-notes","name":"Rich text notes","notes":{"kind":"markdown"},"fields":[],"source":"function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }","version":1,"apiVersion":1,"description":"Edit moment and stack notes visually, storing portable Markdown. Hover cards render safe headings, emphasis, lists, code and HTTPS links. HTML and images are not executed."}},{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"moment-headings","name":"Headings","fields":[{"kind":"heading","label":"Heading level","metadataKey":"headingLevel"},{"kind":"font","label":"Heading font","metadataKey":"headingFont"}],"marker":{"kind":"heading","metadataKey":"headingLevel"},"targets":["moments"],"version":1,"apiVersion":1,"description":"Let a moment act as a heading or marker: only its title shows, sized as a heading from level 1 to 6, and the title is what you click. Choose its font (Times New Roman by default). Headings still group into summaries with other moments."}},{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"moment-colors","name":"Moment colors","fields":[{"kind":"color","label":"Moment color","metadataKey":"color"}],"marker":{"kind":"color","metadataKey":"color"},"source":"function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.color(api.get(\"color\")); }","version":2,"apiVersion":1,"description":"Choose muted semantic swatches or a custom color for moments and stack entries while preserving their white borders."}},{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"dating-context","name":"Dating context","fields":[{"kind":"text","label":"Date precision","metadataKey":"datePrecision"},{"kind":"multiline","label":"Coordinate convention","metadataKey":"coordinateConvention"}],"source":"function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }","version":1,"apiVersion":1,"description":"Explain the precision and coordinate convention of a moment. An exact stored coordinate can still represent an approximate age or a calendar-day marker."}},{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"historical-dates","name":"Historical dates","fields":[{"kind":"text","label":"Original historical date","metadataKey":"historicalDate"},{"kind":"text","label":"Original calendar","metadataKey":"calendar"}],"source":"function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }","version":1,"apiVersion":1,"description":"Retain an original historical date and its calendar separately from the timeline coordinate and display calendar, such as a Julian date on a Gregorian timeline."}},{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"expand-on-hover","name":"Expand on hover","fields":[],"source":"function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.expand(); }","summary":{"kind":"radial"},"version":1,"apiVersion":1,"description":"Hover or focus a summary of two to five moments to fan out its members radially for individual inspection. Larger summaries stay collapsed."}},{"enabled":true,"manifest":{"id":"timeline-theme","name":"Timeline theme","theme":{"halo":"haloColor","text":"textColor","marker":"markerColor","measure":"measureColor","duration":"durationColor","textFont":"textFont","background":"backgroundColor","measureFont":"measureFont"},"fields":[],"version":1,"settings":[{"key":"textColor","kind":"color","label":"Label color"},{"key":"textFont","kind":"font","label":"Label font"},{"key":"measureColor","kind":"color","label":"Measure color"},{"key":"measureFont","kind":"font","label":"Measure font"},{"key":"haloColor","kind":"color","label":"Halo color"},{"key":"markerColor","kind":"color","label":"Marker color"},{"key":"durationColor","kind":"color","label":"Duration color"},{"key":"backgroundColor","kind":"color","label":"Background color"}],"apiVersion":1,"description":"Choose the timeline's colors and fonts: its labels, its measure (the axis, tick marks and their times), the halo that keeps them readable over images, the default marker and duration colors, and a background color. Set them here in the plugin list; anything left blank keeps the usual look, and colors chosen for events still win."},"settings":{"textFont":"'Trebuchet MS', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif","haloColor":"#07080f","textColor":"#e9e6da","markerColor":"#ffe81f","measureColor":"#ffe81f","durationColor":"#2c3450","backgroundColor":"#07080f"}}],"tags":["fiction","star wars","chronology","canon","legends"],"events":[{"id":"a-new-dawn","time":"-347133600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Kanan meets Hera","description":"A former Padawan working as a cargo hauler joins a Twi'lek pilot against an Imperial plot on Gorse.\n\n*A New Dawn (2014)*"}},{"id":"acolyte","time":"-4165603200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Jedi Masters murdered","description":"A former Padawan investigates killings of Jedi that lead back to a witches' coven on Brendok and a hidden Sith.\n\n*The Acolyte (2024)*","datePrecision":"About a century before The Phantom Menace."}},{"id":"ahsoka","time":"347133600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Ahsoka hunts for Thrawn","description":"Ahsoka Tano follows a star map to another galaxy, where Ezra and Thrawn have been since Lothal.\n\n*Ahsoka (2023)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"ahsoka-novel","time":"-568036800/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Ahsoka hides on Raada","description":"A year after Order 66, Ahsoka lives under a false name until the Empire arrives.\n\n*Ahsoka (2016)*"}},{"id":"alliance-canon","time":"-63115200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"The Rebel Alliance is formed","description":"Mon Mothma breaks with the Senate and calls the scattered rebel cells to unite.\n\n*Star Wars Rebels, season 3 (2017)*"}},{"id":"alliances","time":"-63115200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Thrawn and Vader on Batuu","description":"The Emperor sends Thrawn and Vader together after a disturbance in the Force, recalling a time Thrawn met Anakin Skywalker.\n\n*Thrawn: Alliances (2018)*"}},{"id":"andor","time":"-157788000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Cassian Andor and the Aldhani heist","description":"A thief is drawn into the rebellion by Luthen Rael; the heist on Aldhani and the prison on Narkina 5.\n\n*Andor (2022–2025)*","datePrecision":"Season 1 is 5 BBY; season 2 runs to the eve of Rogue One."}},{"id":"aphra","time":"31557600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Doctor Aphra","description":"Vader's former archaeologist, with two murderous droids, stays one step ahead of everyone she cheated.\n\n*Doctor Aphra (2016–2019)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"ascendancy","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Thrawn in the Chiss Ascendancy","description":"Before his exile, Thrawn rises in the Chiss Defense Fleet as the Unknown Regions turn dangerous.\n\n*Thrawn Ascendancy: Chaos Rising, Greater Good and Lesser Evil (2020–2021)*","datePrecision":"Approximate: the trilogy spans his years in the Ascendancy, up to around the end of the Clone Wars."}},{"id":"bad-batch","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"The Bad Batch go rogue","description":"A squad of defective clones refuses the new Empire and protects a young clone, Omega.\n\n*Star Wars: The Bad Batch (2021–2024)*","datePrecision":"Spans 19–18 BBY."}},{"id":"bakura","time":"126230400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The truce at Bakura","description":"Days after Endor, rebels and Imperials join to fight the invading Ssi-ruuk.\n\n*Truce at Bakura (1993)*"}},{"id":"bastion","time":"599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Peace with the Imperial Remnant","description":"The New Republic and the Imperial Remnant sign the Bastion Accords, ending the Galactic Civil War.\n\n*Vision of the Future (1998)*"}},{"id":"battlefront","time":"126230400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Iden Versio and Operation Cinder","description":"An Imperial commando watches Endor fall, then turns against the Emperor's posthumous order to devastate worlds.\n\n*Star Wars Battlefront II (2017)*"}},{"id":"bloodline","time":"883612800/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Leia's parentage is revealed","description":"The Senate learns Leia is Vader's daughter, and she begins to build the Resistance.\n\n*Bloodline (2016)*"}},{"id":"boba-fett","time":"284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Boba Fett rules Mos Espa","description":"Having survived the Sarlacc, Boba Fett takes Jabba's throne.\n\n*The Book of Boba Fett (2021–2022)*"}},{"id":"bounty-hunter-game","time":"-1009843200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Jango Fett hunts the Bando Gora","description":"The hunt that earns Jango the job of template for the Republic's clone army.\n\n*Star Wars: Bounty Hunter (2002)*"}},{"id":"bounty-hunters","time":"110451600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"The War of the Bounty Hunters","description":"Han's frozen body is stolen from Boba Fett on the way to Jabba, and the galaxy's hunters fight over it.\n\n*War of the Bounty Hunters (2021)*"}},{"id":"cade","time":"4323391200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Cade Skywalker","description":"A descendant of Luke, turned bounty hunter, is drawn back into the war against Krayt.\n\n*Star Wars: Legacy (2006–2010)*"}},{"id":"caedus","time":"1262304000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Jacen Solo becomes Darth Caedus","description":"Jacen kills Mara Jade Skywalker and takes the name Darth Caedus.\n\n*Legacy of the Force: Sacrifice (2007)*"}},{"id":"choices-of-one","time":"21038400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Thrawn meets Luke and Mara Jade","description":"The Emperor's Hand and the Rebellion converge on a world under threat from the warlord Nuso Esva.\n\n*Choices of One (2011)*"}},{"id":"clone-wars-2003","time":"-662709600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Clone Wars (the micro-series)","description":"Genndy Tartakovsky's animated shorts follow the war to the eve of Revenge of the Sith, introducing General Grievous and Asajj Ventress.\n\n*Star Wars: Clone Wars (2003–2005)*","datePrecision":"Spans the war."}},{"id":"coruscant-taken","time":"220903200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The New Republic takes Coruscant","description":"Rogue Squadron goes undercover to bring down the capital's shields.\n\n*X-wing: Wedge's Gamble (1996)*"}},{"id":"courtship","time":"252460800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Han and Leia marry","description":"Han kidnaps Leia to Dathomir to win her back from a Hapan prince.\n\n*The Courtship of Princess Leia (1994)*"}},{"id":"crait","time":"1072958400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Crait","description":"The Resistance is nearly wiped out; Luke projects himself across the galaxy to save them, and dies.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode VIII – The Last Jedi (2017)*"}},{"id":"crimson-empire","time":"347133600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Kir Kanos and the Crimson Empire","description":"The last of the Emperor's Royal Guard hunts the traitor among them.\n\n*Crimson Empire (1997–1998)*"}},{"id":"dark-disciple","time":"-631152000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Ventress and Quinlan Vos hunt Dooku","description":"The Jedi Council sanctions an assassination; a story written for The Clone Wars and told as a novel.\n\n*Dark Disciple (2015)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"dark-empire","time":"315576000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"The Emperor reborn","description":"Palpatine returns in clone bodies, and Luke goes to his side to destroy him from within.\n\n*Dark Empire (1991–1992)*"}},{"id":"dark-forces","time":"-946728/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Kyle Katarn and the Death Star plans","description":"In the Legends telling, a mercenary steals the Death Star plans from Danuta.\n\n*Star Wars: Dark Forces (1995)*"}},{"id":"dark-forces-2","time":"157788000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Kyle Katarn and the Valley of the Jedi","description":"Kyle Katarn learns the ways of the Force and stops seven Dark Jedi.\n\n*Star Wars Jedi Knight: Dark Forces II (1997)*"}},{"id":"endor","time":"126230400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","legends","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Endor","description":"The second Death Star is destroyed; Vader saves his son and kills the Emperor.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode VI – Return of the Jedi (1983)*"}},{"id":"exar-kun","time":"-126104169600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Exar Kun falls on Yavin 4","description":"The Great Sith War ends when the Jedi trap the fallen Jedi Exar Kun in his temples on the jungle moon.\n\n*Tales of the Jedi: Dark Lords of the Sith and The Sith War (1994–1996)*"}},{"id":"exegol","time":"1104516000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Exegol","description":"Palpatine returns and is destroyed by Rey, with Ben Solo at her side.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode IX – The Rise of Skywalker (2019)*"}},{"id":"exile","time":"-124684077600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"The Jedi Exile faces the Sith Triumvirate","description":"Five years later, a Jedi cut off from the Force helps rebuild the nearly destroyed Order.\n\n*Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II – The Sith Lords (2004)*"}},{"id":"fallen-order","time":"-441806400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Cal Kestis and the Jedi holocron","description":"A Padawan who survived Order 66 hunts for a list of Force-sensitive children, pursued by the Inquisitors.\n\n*Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order (2019)*"}},{"id":"fallen-star","time":"-7289805600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The fall of Starlight Beacon","description":"The Nihil sabotage the beacon and the Nameless prey on the Jedi; the station falls into Eiram's sea.\n\n*The High Republic: The Fallen Star (2022)*"}},{"id":"fate","time":"1356976800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Lost Tribe of the Sith, and Abeloth","description":"Luke is exiled and searches for the cause of Jedi madness; a forgotten Sith tribe and an ancient being emerge.\n\n*Fate of the Jedi (2009–2012)*"}},{"id":"force-unleashed","time":"-63115200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"The Corellian Treaty","description":"Vader's secret apprentice, Galen Marek, gathers the rebel leaders and dies so they can escape; they found the Rebel Alliance.\n\n*Star Wars: The Force Unleashed (2008)*"}},{"id":"geonosis","time":"-694267200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","legends","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Geonosis","description":"The Republic's new clone army rescues the Jedi on Geonosis, and the Clone Wars begin; Anakin and Padmé marry in secret.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode II – Attack of the Clones (2002)*"}},{"id":"great-disaster","time":"-7321363200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Great Hyperspace Disaster","description":"A starliner breaks apart in hyperspace and its fragments rain on the Hetzal system; the Jedi save who they can, and the Nihil emerge.\n\n*The High Republic: Light of the Jedi (2021)*"}},{"id":"holiday","time":"31557600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Life Day on Kashyyyk","description":"Han Solo races to get Chewbacca home for the Wookiee holiday; Boba Fett's first appearance is in its cartoon.\n\n*The Star Wars Holiday Special (1978)*"}},{"id":"hoth","time":"94672800/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","legends","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Hoth","description":"The Empire breaks the rebel base; Han is frozen in carbonite, and Vader tells Luke he is his father.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode V – The Empire Strikes Back (1980)*"}},{"id":"hyperspace-war","time":"-157788000000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"The Great Hyperspace War","description":"Two hyperspace explorers stumble on the Sith Empire; Naga Sadow invades the Republic and is driven back, and the Empire is broken.\n\n*Tales of the Jedi: The Golden Age of the Sith and The Fall of the Sith Empire (1996–1997)*"}},{"id":"infinite-empire","time":"-813965176800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"The Infinite Empire reaches Tython","description":"The Rakatan Infinite Empire's slave-raiding fleets find the Je'daii's world.\n\n*Dawn of the Jedi (2012–2013)*"}},{"id":"invincible","time":"1293861600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Jaina Solo defeats her brother","description":"Trained by Boba Fett, Jaina kills Caedus, ending the Second Galactic Civil War.\n\n*Legacy of the Force: Invincible (2008)*"}},{"id":"jakku","time":"157788000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Battle of Jakku","description":"The Empire's last fleet falls over a desert world, and the Galactic Concordance ends the war.\n\n*Aftermath: Empire's End (2017)*"}},{"id":"je-daii","time":"-1150369192800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"The Je'daii gather on Tython","description":"Force-sensitives from across the galaxy are drawn to Tython, where the Je'daii learn to keep the light and dark in balance.\n\n*Dawn of the Jedi: Force Storm (2012)*","datePrecision":"Legends dating."}},{"id":"jedha","time":"-12055003200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Battle of Jedha","description":"A peace conference on the holy moon collapses into violence, stirred by the Path of the Open Hand.\n\n*The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha (2022)*"}},{"id":"jedi-academy-game","time":"441806400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Jaden Korr at the Jedi Academy","description":"A student of Kyle Katarn faces the Disciples of Ragnos.\n\n*Star Wars Jedi Knight: Jedi Academy (2003)*"}},{"id":"jedi-outcast","time":"378691200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Kyle Katarn returns to the Force","description":"Kyle Katarn takes up his lightsaber again against the Imperial Remnant and Desann.\n\n*Star Wars Jedi Knight II: Jedi Outcast (2002)*"}},{"id":"kenobi","time":"-284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Obi-Wan Kenobi rescues Leia","description":"Kenobi leaves Tatooine to save a kidnapped ten-year-old Leia, and faces Vader again.\n\n*Obi-Wan Kenobi (2022)*"}},{"id":"kotor-comics","time":"-125094326400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Zayne Carrick, the fugitive Padawan","description":"A Padawan framed for his fellow students' murder by his own masters goes on the run during the Mandalorian Wars.\n\n*Knights of the Old Republic (2006–2010)*"}},{"id":"kylo-ren","time":"883612800/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Ben Solo falls","description":"Luke's new Jedi temple burns, and Ben Solo becomes Kylo Ren.\n\n*The Rise of Kylo Ren (2019–2020)*"}},{"id":"lords-of-sith","time":"-441806400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Vader and the Emperor on Ryloth","description":"Twi'lek rebels ambush the two Sith Lords; Vader and the Emperor fight their way out together.\n\n*Lords of the Sith (2015)*"}},{"id":"lothal","time":"-31557600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"The liberation of Lothal","description":"Ezra frees Lothal and vanishes into hyperspace with Grand Admiral Thrawn.\n\n*Star Wars Rebels, season 4 (2018)*"}},{"id":"mandalore-siege","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"The Siege of Mandalore","description":"Ahsoka captures Maul on Mandalore just as Order 66 is given; she and Rex escape the turned clones.\n\n*Star Wars: The Clone Wars, season 7 (2020)*"}},{"id":"mandalorian","time":"284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Din Djarin takes the Child","description":"A bounty hunter refuses to hand over the child Grogu and protects him across the Outer Rim.\n\n*The Mandalorian (2019–2023)*"}},{"id":"naboo","time":"-1009843200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","legends","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The invasion of Naboo","description":"The Trade Federation blockades Naboo; Qui-Gon Jinn finds Anakin Skywalker on Tatooine and dies fighting Darth Maul; Palpatine becomes Supreme Chancellor.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode I – The Phantom Menace (1999)*"}},{"id":"order-66","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","legends","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"Order 66 and the Galactic Empire","description":"Palpatine turns the clones on the Jedi and declares himself Emperor; Anakin becomes Darth Vader, Padmé dies, and the twins Luke and Leia are hidden.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode III – Revenge of the Sith (2005)*"}},{"id":"ossus","time":"4102488000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"The massacre at Ossus","description":"Darth Krayt's One Sith destroy the Jedi academy and seize the Empire.\n\n*Star Wars: Legacy (2006–2010)*"}},{"id":"outbound-flight","time":"-852055200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Outbound Flight","description":"The Jedi's expedition to another galaxy is destroyed at the edge of known space, where a Chiss commander named Thrawn first meets the Republic.\n\n*Outbound Flight (2006)*"}},{"id":"outlaws","time":"110451600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Kay Vess and the syndicates","description":"A scoundrel plans a heist among the crime syndicates in the year between Hoth and Endor.\n\n*Star Wars Outlaws (2024)*"}},{"id":"plagueis","time":"-1009843200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Sidious kills Darth Plagueis","description":"The Sith master who sought to cheat death is murdered in his sleep by his apprentice, Palpatine.\n\n*Darth Plagueis (2012)*"}},{"id":"praxeum","time":"347133600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Luke founds the Jedi Praxeum","description":"Luke teaches new Jedi in the Massassi temple on Yavin 4, where Exar Kun's spirit lingers.\n\n*The Jedi Academy trilogy (1994)*"}},{"id":"rebels","time":"-157788000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"The Ghost crew on Lothal","description":"Ezra Bridger joins Hera Syndulla's rebel cell, and Kanan Jarrus teaches him to be a Jedi.\n\n*Star Wars Rebels (2014–2018)*"}},{"id":"republic-canon","time":"-788940000000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Jedi Order and the Republic (canon)","description":"Canon places the founding of the Republic and the Jedi Order around twenty-five thousand years before Yavin.\n\n*Star Wars: Timelines (2023)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"republic-commando","time":"-694267200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Delta Squad, from Geonosis to Kashyyyk","description":"Four clone commandos fight the war's hardest missions.\n\n*Star Wars: Republic Commando (2005)*","datePrecision":"Spans 22–19 BBY."}},{"id":"republic-legends","time":"-790612552800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Galactic Republic is founded","description":"The core worlds unite under one Republic, which will last some twenty-five thousand years.\n\n*Legends sourcebooks and novels*","datePrecision":"Legends dating; canon only says the Jedi kept the peace for \"a thousand generations\"."}},{"id":"resistance","time":"1072958400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Kaz Xiono on the Colossus","description":"A young pilot spies on the First Order from an ocean refueling station.\n\n*Star Wars Resistance (2018–2020)*"}},{"id":"revan-novel","time":"-124778750400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Revan goes looking for the true Sith","description":"Revan, his memories returning, sets out beyond known space and is captured by the Sith Emperor.\n\n*The Old Republic: Revan (2011)*"}},{"id":"rogue-one","time":"-631152/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Scarif","description":"Jyn Erso and Cassian Andor steal the Death Star plans at the cost of their lives.\n\n*Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (2016)*"}},{"id":"ruusan","time":"-31557600000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Ruusan, and the Rule of Two","description":"The Brotherhood of Darkness destroys itself on Ruusan; its survivor, Darth Bane, decrees that there shall be only two Sith: a master and an apprentice.\n\n*Darth Bane: Path of Destruction (2006)*"}},{"id":"sacking-coruscant","time":"-115279912800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Sacking of Coruscant","description":"The reborn Sith Empire takes Coruscant by treachery during peace talks, forcing the Treaty of Coruscant.\n\n*Star Wars: The Old Republic – Deceived (2011)*"}},{"id":"shadows","time":"110451600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Shadows of the Empire","description":"Prince Xizor of Black Sun plots to replace Vader at the Emperor's side; Dash Rendar helps the rebels.\n\n*Shadows of the Empire (1996: novel, game and comics)*"}},{"id":"skeleton-crew","time":"284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Lost children and the planet At Attin","description":"Four children are lost in the galaxy after finding a buried starship.\n\n*Star Wars: Skeleton Crew (2024–2025)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"solo","time":"-315576000/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"Han meets Chewbacca and Lando","description":"A young Han Solo joins a crew of thieves, wins the Millennium Falcon from Lando Calrissian and makes the Kessel Run.\n\n*Solo: A Star Wars Story (2018)*","datePrecision":"Its prologue starts in 13 BBY."}},{"id":"splinter","time":"63115200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Luke and Leia on Mimban","description":"The first Star Wars novel after the film: a crash on a swamp world and the hunt for the Kaiburr crystal.\n\n*Splinter of the Mind's Eye (1978)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"squadrons","time":"142009200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Vanguard Squadron and Project Starhawk","description":"Rebel and Imperial pilots fly against each other in the last year of the war.\n\n*Star Wars: Squadrons (2020)*","datePrecision":"Approximate: after Endor."}},{"id":"star-by-star","time":"852055200/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Anakin Solo dies at Myrkr","description":"A Jedi strike team destroys the voxyn queen; Anakin Solo gives his life, and Coruscant falls to the Vong.\n\n*The New Jedi Order: Star by Star (2001)*"}},{"id":"star-forge","time":"-124841865600/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Revan defeats Malak at the Star Forge","description":"A Jedi with no memory learns they were once Darth Revan, and ends the Jedi Civil War over the Rakatan factory station.\n\n*Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic (2003)*","datePrecision":"The player chooses light or dark; Legends follows the light-side ending."}},{"id":"starkiller","time":"1072958400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"Starkiller Base fires","description":"The First Order destroys the Republic's capital; Rey finds Luke Skywalker, and Han is killed by his son.\n\n*Star Wars: Episode VII – The Force Awakens (2015)*"}},{"id":"starlight","time":"-7321363200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Starlight Beacon is dedicated","description":"The Republic opens its great station on the Outer Rim, a symbol of the age.\n\n*The High Republic: The Rising Storm (2021)*"}},{"id":"survivor","time":"-284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"Cal Kestis on Koboh","description":"Five years on, Cal searches for Tanalorr, a planet hidden from the Empire.\n\n*Star Wars Jedi: Survivor (2023)*"}},{"id":"swtor","time":"-114964336800/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","video game"],"color":"#6fd08c","title":"The Old Republic and the Sith Empire in a cold war","description":"The online game's class stories begin a decade into the uneasy peace, before open war resumes.\n\n*Star Wars: The Old Republic (2011)*","datePrecision":"Approximate: the class stories span several years."}},{"id":"tales-empire","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Barriss Offee and Morgan Elsbeth","description":"Two women made by the Clone Wars: a Nightsister seeking revenge, and a fallen Jedi recruited by the Inquisitors.\n\n*Tales of the Empire (2024)*","datePrecision":"Its episodes span the Clone Wars to the New Republic."}},{"id":"tales-jedi-ahsoka","time":"-1136073600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Ahsoka is born on Shili","description":"The anthology follows Ahsoka from infancy and Count Dooku from Jedi Master to Sith.\n\n*Tales of the Jedi (2022)*","datePrecision":"Its episodes span 36–19 BBY."}},{"id":"tales-jedi-dooku","time":"-1009843200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Dooku leaves the Jedi Order","description":"After Qui-Gon Jinn's death, Dooku renounces the Order and becomes Darth Tyranus.\n\n*Tales of the Jedi (2022)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"tales-underworld","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Asajj Ventress and Cad Bane","description":"An assassin starts again, and a young Cad Bane faces the marshal who will hunt him.\n\n*Tales of the Underworld (2025)*","datePrecision":"Approximate: its episodes span Bane's youth to after the Clone Wars."}},{"id":"tcw","time":"-694267200/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"The Clone Wars (the series)","description":"Anakin takes a Padawan, Ahsoka Tano, and the war is fought across the galaxy over seven seasons.\n\n*Star Wars: The Clone Wars (2008–2020)*","datePrecision":"Spans 22–19 BBY."}},{"id":"thrawn","time":"284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Grand Admiral Thrawn returns","description":"An alien tactician leads the remnant of the Empire against the New Republic; Luke meets Mara Jade, and Leia gives birth to the twins Jaina and Jacen.\n\n*Heir to the Empire, Dark Force Rising and The Last Command (1991–1993)*"}},{"id":"thrawn-novel","time":"-284018400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Thrawn joins the Empire","description":"Found on a wild world, Thrawn is brought to Coruscant and rises from cadet to Grand Admiral.\n\n*Thrawn (2017)*","datePrecision":"Approximate: the novel spans the years up to 2 BBY."}},{"id":"treason","time":"-31557600/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"Thrawn and the Death Star","description":"Thrawn's TIE Defender program competes with the Death Star for resources, and a Chiss envoy comes to find him.\n\n*Thrawn: Treason (2019)*","datePrecision":"Approximate."}},{"id":"unifying-force","time":"915170400/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Yuuzhan Vong War ends","description":"The war ends on Coruscant and the living planet Zonama Sekot.\n\n*The New Jedi Order: The Unifying Force (2003)*"}},{"id":"union","time":"631152000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Luke marries Mara Jade","description":"The Jedi Master marries the Emperor's former Hand.\n\n*Union (1999–2000)*"}},{"id":"vader-kyber","time":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Vader bleeds his kyber crystal","description":"Vader takes a Jedi's lightsaber and turns its crystal red.\n\n*Darth Vader: Dark Lord of the Sith (2017–2018)*"}},{"id":"vader-learns","time":"15778800/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","comic"],"color":"#e8835f","title":"Vader learns his son's name","description":"Boba Fett tells Vader that the pilot who destroyed the Death Star is named Skywalker.\n\n*Darth Vader (2015)*","datePrecision":"Between A New Hope and The Empire Strikes Back."}},{"id":"vector-prime","time":"788940000/1","metadata":{"tags":["legends","novel"],"color":"#c58be0","title":"The Yuuzhan Vong invade; Chewbacca dies","description":"Extragalactic invaders who shun technology arrive; Chewbacca dies when a moon falls on Sernpidal.\n\n*The New Jedi Order: Vector Prime (1999)*"}},{"id":"visions","time":"0/1","metadata":{"tags":["non-canon","tv"],"color":"#6fb0e0","title":"Star Wars: Visions","description":"Animation studios from around the world tell their own Star Wars stories, each its own continuity.\n\n*Star Wars: Visions (2021–)*","datePrecision":"Undated: Visions stands outside canon and Legends; placed at the Battle of Yavin for reference."}},{"id":"yavin","time":"0/1","metadata":{"tags":["canon","legends","film"],"color":"#e8c547","title":"The Battle of Yavin","description":"Luke Skywalker destroys the Death Star. The galaxy's calendar counts years before and after this battle (BBY and ABY).\n\n*Star Wars: Episode IV – A New Hope (1977)*"}}],"durations":[{"id":"old-republic-legends","end":"-31557600000/1","start":"-790612552800/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","legends"],"color":"#5a3c3c","title":"The Old Republic","description":"From the Republic's founding to Ruusan, in the Legends reckoning."}},{"id":"mandalorian-wars","end":"-124968096000/1","start":"-125473017600/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","legends"],"color":"#5a3c3c","title":"The Mandalorian Wars","description":"Fought for the Republic by Revan and Malak against Jedi orders."}},{"id":"jedi-civil-war","end":"-124841865600/1","start":"-124936538400/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","legends"],"color":"#5a3c3c","title":"The Jedi Civil War","description":"Revan and Malak return as Sith."}},{"id":"great-galactic-war","end":"-115279912800/1","start":"-116163525600/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","legends"],"color":"#5a3c3c","title":"The Great Galactic War","description":"The reborn Sith Empire against the Republic, ending in the Treaty of Coruscant."}},{"id":"high-republic","end":"-3155760000/1","start":"-15778800000/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","canon"],"color":"#33415f","title":"The High Republic","description":"The Republic and the Jedi at their height, before the Nihil and the Nameless."}},{"id":"clone-wars","end":"-599594400/1","start":"-694267200/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","canon","legends"],"color":"#33415f","title":"The Clone Wars","description":"The Republic's clone army against the Separatists."}},{"id":"empire","end":"126230400/1","start":"-599594400/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","canon","legends"],"color":"#33415f","title":"The Galactic Empire","description":"From Palpatine's proclamation to his death at Endor."}},{"id":"civil-war","end":"157788000/1","start":"-63115200/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","canon"],"color":"#33415f","title":"The Galactic Civil War","description":"From the Alliance's founding to the Galactic Concordance after Jakku."}},{"id":"new-republic","end":"1072958400/1","start":"157788000/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","canon"],"color":"#33415f","title":"The New Republic","description":"Until the Hosnian system is destroyed."}},{"id":"vong-war","end":"915170400/1","start":"788940000/1","metadata":{"tags":["era","legends"],"color":"#5a3c3c","title":"The 